<BaseLayout title="Backup Perplexity Threads" description="Save your Perplexity threads locally with TotalRecalls.">
  <h1>Backing Up Perplexity Threads</h1>
  <p>TotalRecalls exports every Perplexity thread—including multi-turn follow-ups—into your local library.</p>
  
  <h2>Setup</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <a href="https://perplexity.ai">perplexity.ai</a> in your browser and sign in.</li>
    <li>Launch TotalRecalls. Select <strong>"Perplexity"</strong> as the provider.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Scan Threads</strong>. TotalRecalls detects recent and saved threads.</li>
    <li>Choose which threads to export.</li>
    <li>Select <strong>Markdown + JSON</strong> and pick a folder.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Export</strong>.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Rename Collections</h2>
  <p>While scanning, TotalRecalls preserves your labeled thread collections. You can rename them during export to match your local folder structure.</p>
</BaseLayout>
